      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hello, jwata@! Thanks for caffeinating `autoninja` for me a while back. I\u0027m looking into caffeinating `fetch`, realized I\u0027d need to wrap more `subprocess` endpoints with caffeination, and wrapping `subprocess.run` might get confusing since `caffeinate.run` already exists as a call to a _different_ `subprocess` helper. So I want to rename the existing wrapper to match the name (and behavior) of the part of `subprocess` it calls into.\n\nI manually ran `tests/autoninja_test.py` and `tests/siso_test.py` to test this. There was one failure in `autoninja_test.py`, which appears to be a bug in that test case (see https://g-issues.chromium.org/issues/462518292); other tests pass. I don\u0027t know what additional testing I can or should do to prove this works as intended.",
